💡 **SUGGESTION: `artefactBuildTag` / `artefactBuildReleaseName` / `artefactResolveRepository` are duplicated verbatim in two test files**

This PR hoists the releaseArtefacts mock helpers to file level in **both** `test_restoreFromReleases.js` (lines 14–32) and `test_timerAutoCommitAndSave.js` (lines 16–34) — the three template/repository helpers are byte-for-byte identical copies:

```js
function artefactBuildTag(ticketKey, template) {
    var t = (template || 'ai-{ticketKey}').replace(/\{ticketKey\}/g, ticketKey);
    return t.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9._/-]/g, '-');
}
// artefactBuildReleaseName / artefactResolveRepository: same duplication
```

Only `recordingDownloadArtefact` vs `recordingUploadRawFile` genuinely differ (download vs upload contract). If the mock's tag-normalization rules ever change (e.g. a new releaseArtefacts rule), both copies must be edited in lockstep and nothing ties them together. A tiny shared fixture module (e.g. `js/unit-tests/_fixtures/releaseArtefactsMock.js`, loaded via the existing `run_*.json` file lists or `loadModule`) would keep the two harnesses in sync. Not blocking — each test file is deliberately self-contained today, and every copy is now pinned by its own characterization suite.

